WEBVTT

0
00:00:06.219 --> 00:00:06.659
Today,

1
00:00:06.809 --> 00:00:11.000
we're going to explore the fascinating world of energy transformations.

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.239
Energy is all around us,

3
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.559
and it can change from one form to another in many amazing ways.

4
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.399
Let's dive in and see some examples.

5
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:23.510
Chemical to thermal energy.

6
00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:27.680
When we light a candle,

7
00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:30.559
the process transforms chemical energy stored in

8
00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:32.909
the wax into thermal energy or heat.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.669
Similarly,

10
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.479
lighting a sparkler converts the chemical energy in

11
00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:43.200
its composition to both heat and light,

12
00:00:43.599 --> 00:00:46.560
demonstrating how energy stored in chemicals can

13
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.319
be released as warmth and illumination.

14
00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:53.360
Thermal to chemical energy.

15
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.770
Cooking an egg is an example of thermal energy transforming into chemical energy.

16
00:01:00.569 --> 00:01:04.519
The heat from cooking changes the structure of proteins in the egg,

17
00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:07.019
turning it from liquid to solid.

18
00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:12.010
This process shows how heat can cause chemical changes in matter,

19
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.190
specifically altering the proteins,

20
00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.510
bonds and structures.

21
00:01:17.139 --> 00:01:18.709
Light to chemical energy.

22
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.800
Photosynthesis is a process where plants convert

23
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.779
light energy from the sun into chemical energy

24
00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:27.319
stored in glucose,

25
00:01:27.559 --> 00:01:28.819
a type of sugar.

26
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.540
This transformation is crucial for the plant's growth

27
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.699
and is a fundamental example of how light can be converted into chemical energy.

28
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.360
Kinetic to light energy.

29
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.190
Activating a glow stick initiates a chemical reaction

30
00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:48.360
that converts chemical energy into light energy.

31
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.120
The kinetic energy from bending and shaking the stick triggers this reaction,

32
00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:57.180
producing visible light without the need for an external power source.

33
00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.110
Elastic to kinetic energy.

34
00:02:03.019 --> 00:02:05.660
When we stretch and then release a rubber band,

35
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.899
the stored elastic potential energy is transformed into kinetic energy,

36
00:02:11.139 --> 00:02:13.360
propelling the rubber band forward.

37
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.580
This demonstrates how energy stored in stretched materials

38
00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:19.740
can be converted into motion.

39
00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.320
Kinetic to elastic potential energy

40
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.740
and vice versa.

41
00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.210
Pulling back a bow

42
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.610
stores your arm's movement energy as elastic potential energy in the bow's string.

43
00:02:35.229 --> 00:02:39.869
Releasing it transforms this stored energy back into kinetic energy,

44
00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.690
propelling the arrow forward.

45
00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.660
Stretching a rubber band converts kinetic energy from your hands

46
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.100
into elastic potential energy within the band.

47
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.669
Letting go releases this energy,

48
00:02:54.929 --> 00:02:57.410
snapping the band back into place.

49
00:02:59.149 --> 00:03:02.990
Winding up a toy stores kinetic energy from your hand,

50
00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:07.029
turning into elastic potential energy in the toy's spring.

51
00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:12.550
Releasing it sets the toy in motion as the energy converts back.

52
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.600
Pumping air into a balloon stretches it,

53
00:03:16.839 --> 00:03:19.220
storing elastic potential energy.

54
00:03:20.839 --> 00:03:25.940
Releasing the balloon allows it to convert this energy back into kinetic energy,

55
00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.419
making it fly.

56
00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.770
Pulling on a Newton metre

57
00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:35.470
converts kinetic energy into elastic potential energy in its spring.

58
00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:40.070
Releasing it demonstrates how the spring converts elastic potential energy

59
00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.110
back into kinetic energy,

60
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.490
showcasing energy transformation.

61
00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.600
Kinetic to gravitational potential energy

62
00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:50.240
and vice versa.

63
00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:53.380
Pushing a car up a ramp

64
00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.820
stores kinetic energy as gravitational potential energy at the top.

65
00:03:58.279 --> 00:03:59.630
When the car is released,

66
00:03:59.919 --> 00:04:04.619
this potential energy converts back into kinetic energy as it speeds down.

67
00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.929
Another example is Newton's cradle,

68
00:04:09.139 --> 00:04:12.460
which shows how energy transfers between objects,

69
00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.440
converting kinetic energy

70
00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.899
to potential energy and back

71
00:04:17.048 --> 00:04:19.238
as the balls swing back and forth.

72
00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.279
The motion of one ball

73
00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:23.850
transfers energy through the others,

74
00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.079
demonstrating continuous energy conversion.

75
00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:33.429
Energy is constantly changing forms all around us,

76
00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:36.829
and these are just a few examples of how it happens.

77
00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:38.760
As you go about your day,

78
00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.260
see if you can spot more energy transformations in action.

79
00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:44.769
Thanks for watching.

80
00:04:45.089 --> 00:04:46.109
See you next time.

81
00:04:52.359 --> 00:04:54.079
Don't forget to subscribe.